course: dictionary
lesson: 7727
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Puffer is one of them. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer means. «It was reported that a picture of the Pope in a giant white puffer coat went viral and fooled many people.» The words coat, giant and white point to a puffer jacket, a warm padded coat.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit here? In «The puffer blew itself up into a spiky ball to scare off the shark», the clues blew itself up, spiky and shark show that a puffer is a fish. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: The clues can also be about health. A pupil with asthma may need a puffer at school, a small device that puffs medicine into the lungs. The word is the same, but the meaning is different, so always check the clues before you decide.
fact: Puffer is a noun with four main meanings: a pufferfish, an inhaler, a puffer jacket, and an old steam boat or train.
fact: A pufferfish blows itself up into a ball, often covered in spikes, to scare away enemies; many are poisonous to eat.
fact: An inhaler is a small device that puffs medicine into your lungs, used for asthma (in the UK, Australia and New Zealand).
fact: A puffer jacket is a warm, padded coat with puffy stuffed sections.
fact: Phrases to know: «puffer fish», «blue puffer», «puffer jacket».
exercise: «The puffer blew itself up into a spiky ball to scare off the shark.» Which word helps show that puffer means a fish? | steam | *shark | inhaler | coat
exercise: Ruby's friend uses a puffer at school when her chest feels tight. What is a puffer here? | *A small device that puffs medicine into the lungs | A padded winter coat | A steam train | A fish covered in spikes
exercise: «The white puffer coat kept the old man warm all through the snowy walk.» What does puffer mean here? | *A puffer jacket, a warm padded coat | A pufferfish | An inhaler | A small steam boat
test: «She wrapped up in her puffer and sat on the bench, watching the snow fall.» What does puffer mean here? | A steam train | An inhaler | *A puffer jacket | A pufferfish
test: «Ben took a puff from his puffer when his chest started to wheeze.» What does puffer mean here? | *An inhaler | A pufferfish | A small steam boat | A puffer jacket
exam: «The old puffer chugged slowly along the river, puffing out smoke.» What does puffer mean in this (old) sense? | *A small steam boat | An inhaler | A padded coat | A pufferfish
